          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            is one (or rather: three) of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+groups"} exceptional Lie groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+algebra"} normed algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_2 = Aut(\mathbb{O})
                  \\,.
          %p
            Another way to characterize it is as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(7)
            of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential 3-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle ,(-)\times (-) \rangle
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^7
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Stab
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_2 \simeq Stab_{GL(7)}(\langle -, -\times -\rangle)
                  \\,.
          %p
            As such, the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            is a higher analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            (which is the group that preserves a canonical 2-form on any
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2n}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic geometry
          %h2#Definition Definition
          #As2PlectomorphismsOnR7.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^7
              consider the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 3
