          %h3#relation_to_higher_prequantum_geometry Relation to higher prequantum geometry
          %p
            The 3-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            from def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#As2PlectomorphismsOnR7"}
            we may regard as equipping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^7
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            is the linear subgroup of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectomorphism+group"} 2-plectomorphism group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}^7, \omega)
            in the symplectomorphism group.
          %p
            Or, dually, we may regard the 4-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star \omega
            of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#As2PlectomorphismsOnR7"}
            as being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} 3-plectic structure
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            correspondingly as the linear part in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-plectomorphism+group"} 3-plectomorphism group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^7
          %h3#as_zerodivisors_of_the_sedenions As zero-divisors of the sedenions
          %p
            It is shown in Corollary 2.14 of
            %a{:href => "#Moreno97"} Moreno (1997)
            that the unit-norm
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-divisor"} zero-divisors
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sedenion"} sedenions
            is isomorphic to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi p
                  %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(p, q) \mid p q = 0, |p| = |q| = 1\}
            is diffeomorphic to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            = succeed "-torsors.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
