          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li#SpringerVeltkamp00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tonny+Springer"}> Tonny Springer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ferdinand+Veldkamp"} Ferdinand Veldkamp
              = succeed "," do
                %em Octonions, Jordan Algebras, and Exceptional Groups
          %p Surveys are in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Spiro Karigiannis,
                %em
                  What is… a
                  = succeed "-manifold" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/201104/rtx110400580p.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Salamon"}> Simon Salamon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A tour of exceptional geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://calvino.polito.it/~salamon/G/COR/tour.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G2_%28mathematics%29"} G₂
                \.
          %p The definitions are reviewed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Joyce96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Joyce"}> Dominic Joyce
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Compact Riemannian 7-manifolds with holonomy
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                %strong 43
                2 (1996) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/journal-of-differential-geometry/volume-43/issue-2/Compact-Riemannian-7-manifolds-with-holonomy-G_2-I/10.4310/jdg/1214458109.full"}> doi:10.4310/jdg/1214458109
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/JDG/archive/1996/43-2-291.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Ferolito
              %p
                Ferolito
                %em
                  The octonions and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www2.bc.edu/~reederma/Ferolito.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Baez
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                , section 4.1
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/octonions/node14.html"} G2
                of:
                %em The Octonions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105155"}> arXiv:math/0105155
                )
            %li
              %p
                Ruben Arenas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Constructing a Matrix Representation of the Lie Group
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.hmc.edu/seniorthesis/archives/2005/rarenas/rarenas-2005-thesis.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Ibort
              Alberto Ibort,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multisymplectic geometry: generic and exceptional
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://rsme.es/public/publi3.htm"} Proceedings of the IX Fall workshop on geometry and physics
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/IbortMultisymplectic.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A description of the root space decomposition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_2
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Basak17
              Tathagata Basak,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Root space decomposition of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_2
                  from octonions
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.02367"} 1708.02367
          %p
            As the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-divisor"} zero divisors
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sedenion"} sedenions
          %ul
            %li#Moreno97
              Guillermo Moreno.
              = succeed "." do
                %em The zero divisors of the Cayley-Dickson algebras over the real numbers
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9710013"} doi
          %p Cohomological properties are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Younggi Choi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Homology of the gauge group of exceptional Lie group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Miyaoka93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reiko+Miyaoka"}> Reiko Miyaoka
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The linear isotropy group of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi SO
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2/SO(4)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ojm/1200784357"} Euclid
            %li#Ishiguro
              %p
                Kenshi Ishiguro,
                %em
                  Classifying spaces and a subgroup of the exceptional Lie group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Ishiguro/G2.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Kramer02
              %p
                Linus Kramer, 4.27 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homogeneous Spaces, Tits Buildings, and Isoparametric Hypersurfaces
          %p
            Discussion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            as a subgroup of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
          %ul
            %li#Varadarajan01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veeravalli+Varadarajan"}> Veeravalli Varadarajan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spin(7)-subgroups of SO(8) and Spin(8)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/81114499.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#applications_in_physics Applications in physics
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Ernst-Michael Ilgenfritz, Axel Maas,
              %em
                Topological aspects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                Yang-Mills theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1210.5963"}> arXiv:1210.5963
              )
